der>\n   261→\n   262→    <div class=\"container\">\n   263→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   264→            <!-- Left Column: New Products (40%) -->\n   265→            <section class=\"new-products\">\n   266→                <h2>New Products</h2>\n   267→\n   268→                <div class=\"item\">\n   269→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   270→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/agent-memory-dev\" target=\"_blank\">AgentMemory</a>\n   271→                    </div>\n   272→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   273→                        Persistent memory layer for AI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Windsurf, etc.) that captures, compresses, and indexes agent sessions to provide cross-session context. Reduces token usage by 92% while maintaining searchable memory across coding sessions.\n   274→                    </div>\n   275→                    <div class=\"quote\">The cross-session forgetting problem is real - every AI coding session starts from zero</div>\n   276→                    <div class=\"quote\">Up to 95% fewer tokens per session, 200x more tool calls before hitting context limits</div>\n   277→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   278→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   279→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   280→                        <span>Released: 2026-05-16</span>\n   281→                    </div>\n   282→                </div>\n   283→\n   284→                <div class=\"item\">\n   285→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   286→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/raindrop-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">Raindrop Workshop</a>\n   287→                    </div>\n   288→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   289→                        Open-source, local debugger for AI agents that streams every token and tool call for debugging. First dedicated local debugging tool specifically designed for AI agents with MCP-native integration and one-command installation.\n   290→                    </div>\n   291→                    <div class=\"quote\">First dedicated local debugging tool specifically designed for AI agents</div>\n   292→                    <div class=\"quote\">MCP-native with one-command installation</div>\n   293→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   294→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   295→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   296→                        <span>Released: 2026-05-14</span>\n   297→                    </div>\n   298→                </div>\n   299→\n   300→                <div class=\"item\">\n   301→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   302→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/cline-sdk\" target=\"_blank\">Cline SDK</a>\n   303→                    </div>\n   304→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   305→                        Plugin-based open-source runtime for building coding agents. Allows developers to create custom AI coding agents with a modular, extensible architecture.\n   306→                    </div>\n   307→                    <div class=\"quote\">Build coding agents with a plugin-based open-source runtime</div>\n   308→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   309→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   310→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   311→                        <span>Released: 2026-05-15</span>\n   312→                    </div>\n   313→                </div>\n   314→\n   315→                <div class=\"item\">\n   316→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   317→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/openhuman\" target=\"_blank\">OpenHuman</a>\n   318→                    </div>\n   319→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   320→                        Open-source AI agent/harness with persistent memory across sessions. Local-first, privacy-first with 118+ integrations (Gmail, Slack, Notion, GitHub). Features a Memory Tree system that canonicalizes context and includes a built-in code sandbox.\n   321→                    </div>\n   322→                    <div class=\"quote\">8000+ GitHub stars, 5000+ users in first 7 days</div>\n   323→                    <div class=\"quote\">Reached #1 on Product Hunt daily leaderboard May 15, 2026</div>\n   324→                    <div class=\"quote\">118+ integrations including GitHub with built-in code sandbox</div>\n   325→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   326→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   327→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   328→                        <span>Released: 2026-05-15</span>\n   329→                    </div>\n   330→                </div>\n   331→\n   332→                <div class=\"item\">\n   333→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   334→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/openclaw-os\" target=\"_blank\">OpenClaw OS</a>\n   335→                    </div>\n   336→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   337→                        Turns one-off AI chat sessions into persistent, reusable applications. Open-source tool that converts ephemeral AI agent interactions into usable apps for developers.\n   338→                    </div>\n   339→                    <div class=\"quote\">Turns one-off chats into persistent apps</div>\n   340→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   341→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   342→                        <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   343→                        <span>Released: 2026-05-14</span>\n   344→                    </div>\n   345→                </div>\n   346→            </section>\n   347→\n   348→            <!-- Middle Column: Whitelist Updates (35%) -->\n   349→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   350→                <h2>Whitelist Updates</h2>\n   351→\n   352→                <div class=\"item\">\n   353→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   354→                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a>\n   355→                    </div>\n   356→                    <div class=\"update-subtitle\">Plugin System, Agent View, Background Sessions</div>\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   358→                        Major updates including plugin dependency enforcement, agent view for session management, enhanced background session persistence, and numerous UI/UX improvements. Windows PowerShell tool now enabled by default for Bedrock/Vertex/Foundry users.\n   359→                    </div>\n   360→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   361→                        <span>Released: 2026-05-15</span>\n   362→                    </div>\n   363→                </div>\n   364→\n   365→                <div class=\"item\">\n   366→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   367→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor</a>\n   368→                    </div>\n   369→                    <div class=\"update-subtitle\">Development Environments, Multi-Repo Support, Teams Integration</div>\n   370→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   371→                        May 2026 updates: Development environments for cloud agents with isolated containers, multi-repo environments support, environment configuration as code with Dockerfile improvements, Cursor in Microsoft Teams integration, Bugbot Effort Levels customization, PR Review experience improvements, parallel plan execution, and Split PRs feature.\n   372→                    </div>\n   373→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   374→                        <span>Released: 2026-05-01</span>\n   375→                    </div>\n   376→                </div>\n   377→\n   378→                <div class=\"item\">\n   379→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   380→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot</a>\n   381→                    </div>\n   382→                    <div class=\"update-subtitle\">Copilot App Technical Preview, REST API Support</div>\n   383→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   384→                        May 2026 updates: GitHub Copilot app technical preview (desktop experience for agentic development), REST API support for starting cloud agent tasks, Copilot code review comment experience improvements, Copilot CLI v1.0.45 with /autopilot command, Rubber Duck mode supports more models, C++ code intelligence in public preview, model updates including GPT-5.5 GA and several deprecations.\n   385→                    </div>\n   386→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   387→                        <span>Released: 2026-05-14</span>\n   388→                    </div>\n   389→                </div>\n   390→\n   391→                <div class=\"item\">\n   392→                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n   393→                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.ai/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf</a>\n   394→                    </div>\n   395→                    <div class=\"update-subtitle\">Claude Opus 4.7 Fast Mode, Devin Review Integration</div>\n   396→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   397→                        May 2026 updates: Claude Opus 4.7 (fast mode) with 2.5x higher output speeds, Devin Review and Quick Review available to all users, Agent Command Center improvements (list display, sorting/filtering), Windows bug fixes, MCP server fixes, Devin for Terminal CLI agent written in Rust.\n   398→                    </div>\n   399→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   400→                        <span>Released: 2026-05-12</span>\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                </div>\n   403→            </section>\n   404→\n   405→            <!-- Right Column: Technical Insights (25%) -->\n   406→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   407→                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   408→                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n   409→                    No technical insights available for this date.\n   410→                </div>\n   411→            </section>\n   412→        </main>\n   413→\n   414→        <footer>\n   415→            <a href=\"#\">Archives</a>\n   416→            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   417→            <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a>\n   418→            <a href=\"#\">GitHub</a>\n   419→            <span style=\"color: #828282; font-size: 11px; margin-top: 10px; display: block;\">\n   420→                Generated with Claude Code\n   421→            </span>\n   422→        </footer>\n   423→    </div>\n   424→</body>\n   425→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
