res a Memory Tree system that canonicalizes context and includes a built-in code sandbox.\n   239→                    </div>\n   240→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   241→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   242→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">GitHub Trending</span>\n   243→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   244→                    </div>\n   245→                    <div class=\"stats\">🏆 #1 Product Hunt | ⭐ 12,086+ stars</div>\n   246→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Two-minute setup, no config files, simple GUI anyone can use\"</div>\n   247→                </div>\n   248→\n   249→                <div class=\"item\">\n   250→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/agent-memory-dev\" target=\"_blank\">AgentMemory</a></div>\n   251→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   252→                        Persistent memory layer for AI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Windsurf, etc.) that captures, compresses, and indexes agent sessions to provide cross-session context. Reduces token usage by 92% while maintaining searchable memory.\n   253→                    </div>\n   254→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   255→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   256→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">code agent</span>\n   257→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">memory</span>\n   258→                    </div>\n   259→                    <div class=\"stats\">📉 92% fewer tokens | 100% open source</div>\n   260→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"The cross-session forgetting problem is real - every AI coding session starts from zero\"</div>\n   261→                </div>\n   262→\n   263→                <div class=\"item\">\n   264→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/cline-sdk\" target=\"_blank\">Cline SDK</a></div>\n   265→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   266→                        Plugin-based open-source runtime for building coding agents. Allows developers to create custom AI coding agents with a modular, extensible architecture.\n   267→                    </div>\n   268→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   269→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   270→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   271→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">SDK</span>\n   272→                    </div>\n   273→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Build coding agents with a plugin-based open-source runtime\"</div>\n   274→                </div>\n   275→\n   276→                <div class=\"item\">\n   277→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph\" target=\"_blank\">codegraph</a></div>\n   278→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   279→                        Pre-indexed code knowledge graph for Claude Code that reduces token usage and tool calls. Provides 100% local code understanding with pre-indexed knowledge.\n   280→                    </div>\n   281→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   282→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">GitHub Trending</span>\n   283→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">code agent</span>\n   284→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">#17 trending</span>\n   285→                    </div>\n   286→                    <div class=\"stats\">⭐ 3,053+ stars | 860 stars today</div>\n   287→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Pre-indexed code knowledge graph for Claude Code — fewer tokens, fewer tool calls, 100% local\"</div>\n   288→                </div>\n   289→\n   290→                <div class=\"item\">\n   291→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/tech-leads-club/agent-skills\" target=\"_blank\">agent-skills</a></div>\n   292→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   293→                        Secure, validated skill registry for professional AI coding agents. Extends Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot and more with validated, secure skills.\n   294→                    </div>\n   295→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   296→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">GitHub Trending</span>\n   297→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">code agent</span>\n   298→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">security</span>\n   299→                    </div>\n   300→                    <div class=\"stats\">⭐ 3,245+ stars</div>\n   301→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Extend Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot and more with absolute confidence\"</div>\n   302→                </div>\n   303→\n   304→                <div class=\"item\">\n   305→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://raindrop.ai/workshop\" target=\"_blank\">Raindrop Workshop</a></div>\n   306→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   307→                        Open-source, local debugger for AI agents that streams every token and tool call for debugging. First dedicated local debugging tool specifically designed for AI agents with MCP-native integration and one-command installation.\n   308→                    </div>\n   309→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   310→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   311→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   312→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">debugger</span>\n   313→                    </div>\n   314→                    <div class=\"stats\">🚀 200+ GitHub stars day 1</div>\n   315→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"First dedicated local debugging tool specifically designed for AI agents\"</div>\n   316→                </div>\n   317→\n   318→                <div class=\"item\">\n   319→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/openclaw-os\" target=\"_blank\">OpenClaw OS</a></div>\n   320→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   321→                        Turns one-off AI chat sessions into persistent, reusable applications. Open-source tool that converts ephemeral AI agent interactions into usable apps for developers.\n   322→                    </div>\n   323→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   324→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   325→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   326→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">persistence</span>\n   327→                    </div>\n   328→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Turns one-off chats into persistent apps\"</div>\n   329→                </div>\n   330→\n   331→                <div class=\"item\">\n   332→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/kilo-code-v7-for-vs-code\" target=\"_blank\">Kilo Code v7 for VS Code</a></div>\n   333→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   334→                        VS Code extension that runs parallel AI agents with diff reviewer and multi-model comparisons. Open source and free.\n   335→                    </div>\n   336→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   337→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   338→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">AI IDE integration</span>\n   339→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">#1 Product Hunt</span>\n   340→                    </div>\n   341→                    <div class=\"stats\">🏆 #1 Product Hunt last week | 147 upvotes</div>\n   342→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"The line level review comments on agent diffs is a really smart UX call\"</div>\n   343→                </div>\n   344→            </section>\n   345→\n   346→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Column -->\n   347→            <section class=\"column\">\n   348→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   349→                    Whitelist Updates <span class=\"item-count\">9</span>\n   350→                </div>\n   351→\n   352→                <div class=\"item\">\n   353→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code: Plugin System, Agent View</a></div>\n   354→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   355→                        Major updates including plugin dependency enforcement, agent view for session management, enhanced background session persistence, and numerous UI/UX improvements. Windows PowerShell tool now enabled by default.\n   356→                    </div>\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   358→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-05-15</span>\n   359→                        <span class=\"update-type\">RELEASE</span>\n   360→                    </div>\n   361→                </div>\n   362→\n   363→                <div class=\"item\">\n   364→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-05-13-start-copilot-cloud-agent-tasks-via-the-rest-api/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: REST API for Cloud Agent Tasks</a></div>\n   365→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   366→                        Copilot Business and Enterprise users can programmatically start Copilot cloud agent tasks with the new Agent tasks REST API, available in public preview. The API makes it easy to weave Copilot into custom automations like refactoring across repositories.\n   367→                    </div>\n   368→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   369→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-05-13</span>\n   370→                        <span class=\"update-type\">RELEASE</span>\n   371→                    </div>\n   372→                </div>\n   373→\n   374→                <div class=\"item\">\n   375→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: Code Review Comment Improvements</a></div>\n   376→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   377→                        Improvements to the code review comment experience in GitHub Copilot for better developer workflow.\n   378→                    </div>\n   379→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   380→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-05-12</span>\n   381→                        <span class=\"update-type\">IMPROVEMENT</span>\n   382→                    </div>\n   383→                </div>\n   384→\n   385→                <div class=\"item\">\n   386→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf: Claude Opus 4.7 Fast Mode</a></div>\n   387→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   388→                        Claude Opus 4.7 (fast mode) now available with ~2.5x higher output speeds. Devin Review and Quick Review available to all users with 2-week free trial. Agent Command Center improvements with list display option and improved sorting/filtering.\n   389→                    </div>\n   390→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   391→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-05-12</span>\n   392→                        <span class=\"update-type\">RELEASE</span>\n   393→                    </div>\n   394→                    <div class=\"stats\">⚡ 2.5x faster output</div>\n   395→                </div>\n   396→\n   397→                <div class=\"item\">\n   398→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf: Devin Review Available to All</a></div>\n   399→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   400→                        Devin Review and Quick Review now available to all Windsurf IDE users with existing subscription. Devin Review includes 2-week free trial for self-serve users. Agent Command Center improvements including list display option and improved sessions sidebar.\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   403→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-05-06</span>\n   404→                        <span class=\"update-type\">RELEASE</span>\n   405→                    </div>\n   406→                </div>\n   407→\n   408→                <div class=\"item\">\n   409→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-05-08-upcoming-deprecation-of-grok-code-fast-1/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: Grok Code Fast 1 Deprecation</a></div>\n   410→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   411→                        Grok Code Fast 1 deprecated across all Copilot experiences (deprecation date: May 15, 2026). Recommended alternatives: GPT-5 mini / Claude Haiku 4.5. Also includes more flexible secrets for Copilot cloud agent.\n   412→                    </div>\n   413→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   414→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-05-08</span>\n   415→                        <span class=\"update-type\">DEPRECATION</span>\n   416→                    </div>\n   417→                </div>\n   418→\n   419→                <div class=\"item\">\n   420→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: Multiple Model Deprecations</a></div>\n   421→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   422→                        Upcoming deprecations including GPT-4.1 and Claude Sonnet 4. Rubber Duck mode in Copilot CLI now supports more models.\n   423→                    </div>\n   424→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   425→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-05-07</span>\n   426→                        <span class=\"update-type\">DEPRECATION</span>\n   427→                    </div>\n   428→                </div>\n   429→\n   430→                <div class=\"item\">\n   431→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: GPT-5.2 Deprecation</a></div>\n   432→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   433→                        Upcoming deprecation of GPT-5.2 and GPT-5.2-Codex models across Copilot experiences.\n   434→                    </div>\n   435→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   436→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-05-01</span>\n   437→                        <span class=\"update-type\">DEPRECATION</span>\n   438→                    </div>\n   439→                </div>\n   440→\n   441→                <div class=\"item\">\n   442→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor: Development Environments & Multi-Repo</a></div>\n   443→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   444→                        Development environments for cloud agents with isolated containers, multi-repo environments support, environment configuration as code with Dockerfile improvements, Cursor in Microsoft Teams integration, Bugbot Effort Levels customization, PR Review improvements, and Split PRs feature.\n   445→                    </div>\n   446→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   447→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-05-01</span>\n   448→                        <span class=\"update-type\">RELEASE</span>\n   449→                    </div>\n   450→                </div>\n   451→            </section>\n   452→\n   453→            <!-- Technical Insights Column -->\n   454→            <section class=\"column\">\n   455→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   456→                    Technical Insights <span class=\"item-count\">5</span>\n   457→                </div>\n   458→\n   459→                <div class=\"item\">\n   460→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/15/\" target=\"_blank\">QR code generator built with Claude</a></div>\n   461→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   462→                        Simon used Claude to build a QR code generator tool for creating scannable codes for URLs, text, or WiFi networks. An example of 'vibe coding' - quickly building practical tools with AI assistance.\n   463→                    </div>\n   464→                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison | 2026-05-15</div>\n   465→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   466→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">tools</span>\n   467→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai</span>\n   468→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                </div>\n   471→\n   472→                <div class=\"item\">\n   473→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/11/\" target=\"_blank\">GitLab Act 2: Restructuring for the agentic era</a></div>\n   474→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   475→                        GitLab announces significant restructuring: reducing countries by 30%, flattening management by removing up to 3 layers, reorganizing into 60 smaller empowered teams. They argue 'the agentic era multiplies demand for software' and that as software production costs collapse, demand will expand.\n   476→                    </div>\n   477→                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison | 2026-05-11</div>\n   478→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   479→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">gitlab</span>\n   480→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n   481→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">startups</span>\n   482→                    </div>\n   483→                </div>\n   484→\n   485→                <div class=\"item\">\n   486→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/11/\" target=\"_blank\">Your AI coding agent needs to reduce maintenance costs</a></div>\n   487→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   488→                        James Shore argues that AI coding agents must reduce maintenance costs to be viable. If you double code output with AI but maintain or increase maintenance costs, you're trading temporary speed for permanent indenture. The math only works if LLMs decrease maintenance costs.\n   489→                    </div>\n   490→                    <div class=\"insight-author\">James Shore (via Simon Willison) | 2026-05-11</div>\n   491→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   492→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai</span>\n   493→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   494→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">maintenance</span>\n   495→                    </div>\n   496→                </div>\n   497→\n   498→                <div class=\"item\">\n   499→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/11/\" target=\"_blank\">Learning on the Shop floor: Shopify's River coding agent</a></div>\n   500→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   501→                        Tobias Lütke describes Shopify's internal coding agent tool, River, which operates entirely in public on their Slack. River doesn't respond to direct messages, insisting on public channels where anyone can watch and learn. This creates a 'Lehrwerkstatt' (teaching workshop) environment where osmosis learning happens.\n   502→                    </div>\n   503→                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison (discussing Tobias Lütke) | 2026-05-11</div>\n   504→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   505→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">shopify</span>\n   506→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   507→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">learning</span>\n   508→                    </div>\n   509→                </div>\n   510→\n   511→                <div class=\"item\">\n   512→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46570115\" target=\"_blank\">LLM coding workflow going into 2026</a></div>\n   513→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   514→                        Hacker News discussion about multi-step AI pipelines for 3D mesh generation with validation stages. Community highlights challenges with LLMs skipping edge cases or taking suboptimal paths, and debates the practical efficiency of AI coding assistance.\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Hacker News Community | 2026-05-10</div>\n   517→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   518→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm</span>\n   519→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   520→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">workflow</span>\n   521→                    </div>\n   522→                </div>\n   523→            </section>\n   524→        </main>\n   525→\n   526→        <footer>\n   527→            <p>\n   528→                <a href=\"#\">↑ Back to top</a> |\n   529→                Report generated by <strong>Agent Code Daily</strong> - Powered by <strong>Claude Agent SDK</strong>\n   530→            </p>\n   531→            <p style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 7pt;\">\n   532→                Last updated: May 17, 2026 | Data sourced from Product Hunt, GitHub Trending, and technical blogs\n   533→            </p>\n   534→        </footer>\n   535→    </div>\n   536→</body>\n   537→</html>"
